                <pb facs="1200" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4960/8.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of the 22d ultimo, reporting your interview with the Sultan on the same
                    day, regarding equal treatment of American institutions, and stating that <pb
                        facs="1201" n="1051" xml:id="pg1051"/> if further obstacles to the
                    fulfillment of His Majesty’s promises arise you will ask the department for
                    further instructions.</p>
                <p>In view of the telegrams exchanged March 5 and 6, the department will await the
                    result of your request for another audience of His Majesty.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(See also correspondence, Increase of Turkish Customs Duties, following.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
